    "chunk_text": "The forest area comprising Lot Numbers 1, 3, 4 and 5 of PP kq 3175 compiled by Sri Lanka Survey Department representingKaramidula, Bambaragama, Agappola, Kithulpe, Bowala and Yakadagoda Villages of Hanguranketa Divisional Secretary\u2019sDivision in Nuwara Eliya District, Central province containing in extent 75.1453 ha. and bounded as follows,\n\nBy East: Agappola Village, Yakodagoda Village, Bambaragama, Yakodagoda Karamidula.Road and Karamidula Village.\n\nBy South : Yakadagoda Village, Bambaragama Road from Karamidula, Bambaragama Village.\n\nBy West: Karamidula Village, Bambaragama Village, Bowala Village, Kithulpe Village.\n\nNote :\n\nLot number 02 (0.1904 ha) is used as a cemetery and has demarcated using boundary pegs.\n\n11-76/1\n\n\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\u2013\n\nFOREST CONSERVATION ORDINANCE\n\nTHE order under Section 3. that has to be read with Section 64. (1) of the Forest Conservation Ordinance (Chapter 451), asNo. 13 of 1966, as amended by Acts, No. 56 of 1979, No. 13 of 1982, No. 84 of 1988, No. 23 of 1995 and No. 65 of 2009 that haveto be read with Section 51 of the 19th amendment of the Constitution of Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe Order\n\nBy virtue of powers vested in me by Section 3.of the Forest Conservation Ordinance (Chapter 451) as amended by Acts,No. 13 of 1966, No. 56 of 1979, No. 13 of 1982, No. 84 of 1988, No. 23 of 1995 and No. 65 of 2009, that have to be read withSection 51 of the 19th amendment of the Constitution of Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka, I, Maithripala Sirisena,President do by this order declare the Rojasangama Forest of 48.066 hectares bounded by the limit set forth in the schedulehereto as Roajasangama Reserved Forest from 12th day of October, 2019.\n\nMAITHRIPALA SIRISENA,\n\nPresident.\n\nPolonnaruwa,12th October, 2019.\n\nRojasangama Forest\n\nSCHEDULE 01"
