    "chunk_text": "wxl 2145$45 - 2019 Tlaf;dan\u00be ui 16 jeks nodod - 2019'10'16\n\nNo. 2145/45 \u2013 WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 16, 2019\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nYS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www. documents.gov.lk1A\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nNotice under Section 7\n\nRef. No.: DIK/LAN/02/30/45.\n\nI, hereby give notice, under Sub-section (1) of Section 7 ofthe Land Acquisition Act, as amended by the LandAcquisition (Amendment) Act, No.28 of 1964, that theGovernment intends to acquire the following Land/Servitudewhich is required for a public purpose mentioned below.\n\nDescription of the Land to be Acquired:\n\nFollowing portion of land depicted in Preliminary SurveyPlan No. MR 2807 prepared by Surveyor General, situated inthe village of Babarende Central in Grama Niladari's Divisionof Babarenda Central 450 D in Divisional Secretary's Divisionof Dickwella in Matara District, Southern Province.\n\n1. Lot No. 1Name of the Land: Galketiyewatta; Description: Open;Claimant : Ramya Kuruppu Nanayakkara of Walawwatta,Pathegama, Kottegoda; Extent: 0.0320 Hectare.\n\n1A - G 31270 - 27 (2019/10)\n\nAll persons interested in the aforesaid land/lands on whicha servitude is to be acquired are hereby required to appearpersonally, or by agents duly authorized in writing, before meat Divisional Secretariat of Dickwella, on the 23rd day ofOctober, 2019 at 10.00 a.m. and are hereby requested to notifyto me in writing (in duplicate) on or before the 16th day ofOctober, 2019 the nature of their interests in the land, theparticulars of their claims for compensation for the acquisitionof the said land/servitude the amount of compensation andthe details of the computation of such amount.\n\nB. S. RANJITHA,Divisional Secretary,\n\nDickwella.\n\nDivisional Secretariat,Dickwella.16th day of September, 2019.\n\n11 - 86"
