    "chunk_text": "4. A Board of not less than three Senior Officers nominated by the respective Service Commanders and InspectorGeneral of Police will examine the recommendations made for the award of the SERVICE MEDAL. The recommendationsof the Board along with the recommendations of the respective Service Commanders and Inspector General of Police willbe forwarded to His Excellency the President through the Secretary of Defence, for His Excellency\u2019s approval. The recom-mendations of the Minister of Defence, the State Minister of Defence and the Secretary of Defence of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka should be sent directly by the Secretary of Defence for His Excellency\u2019s approval.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'10'21PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 21.10.20196A\n\n8. Any Officer of the Sri Lanka Army, Navy, Air Force and Police who is cashiered, dismissed or has been calledupon to resign or retire his Commission, shall forfeit the Medal conferred on him unless His Excellency the Presidentshall direct otherwise.\n\n9. Every Soldier, Seaman, Airman and Policemen who has been discharged from the Army, Navy, Air Force andPolice with disgrace or with ignominy, shall forfeit the Medal unless His Excellency the President shall direct otherwise.\n\n13. In an event where a Medal is lost, and if it is desirous to replace it, such a loss should be reported to the Police.A declaration testified by a Justice of the Peace stating the circumstances under which the loss occurred should be submit-ted along with a copy of the complaint made to the Police. This declaration shall be forwarded to the Commanding Officerwho will forward it to the respective Service Commander through the usual channel of communication. The Medal losttherewith will be replaced on payment if the explanation as to the loss is considered satisfactory.\n