    "chunk_text": "III fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2018'09'17PART III \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 17.09.20181A\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%hThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nw;s \u00fafYI EXTRAORDINARY\n\n(Published by Authority)PART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nwxl 2147$2 \u2013 2019 Tlaf;dan\u00be 28 jeks i\u00f7od \u2013 2019'10'28No. 2147/2 \u2013 MONDAY, OCTOBER 28, 2019\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n1A \u2013 G 31333 \u2013 21 (10/2019)\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nDeclaration under Section 5\n\nI, Gayantha Karunatilleke, Minister of Lands and ParliamentaryReforms, do hereby declare, under Sub-section (1) of Section 5 of theLand Acquisition Act, that the land described below is needed for apublic purpose and will be acquired under the provisions of that Act.\n\nAllotments of Lands in depicted in the Advance Tracing No. KU/IBB/2018/283 dated 30.08.2018 Prepared by the Surveyor - General,situated in Village called Hangamuwa in the Grama Niladari DivisionNo.486, Meddeketiya (FVP 1239) in the Divisional Secretary\u2019sDivision of Ibbagamuwa in Kurunegala District in North WesternProvince and boundaries as follows:\n\n01. Lot No. 1 \u2013 Sabaragamu Idama \u2013 Extent : 0.0924 HectareNorth: Sabaragamu Idama claimed by Sangamu Viharaya andKalagahamulagala claimed by D. Punchinaide; East: Sabaragamu Idamaclaimed by Sangamu Viharaya; South: Sabaragamu Idama claimed bySangamu Viharaya and Lot No. 2; West: Lot No. 2 and SabaragamuIdama claimed by Sangamu Viharaya.\n\n02. Lot No. 2 \u2013 Sabaragamu Idama \u2013 Extent : 0.7625 HectareNorth: Sabaragamu Idama claimed by Sangamu Viharaya and LotNo. 1; East: Lot No. 1 and Sabaragamu Idama claimed by SangamuViharaya; South: Lot No. 3, Sabaragamu Idama claimed by SangamuViharaya, Lot Nos. 4 and 5; West: Lot No. 5 and Sabaragamu Idamaclaimed by Sangamu Viharaya."
